{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"paternal-repayable-flamingo","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\n\nDaily plan-review cache reads in `.rebar/usage.jsonl` went from ~80% of input tokens (2026-08-06..11) to 0 from 2026-08-12 onward, and the median full plan review went from about $2.18 to about $4.82 (Aug 6–29 logged spend is roughly $3,000, of which finders alone are ~358M uncached Opus input tokens). The change coincides with commit `6d4f394195b2` (2026-08-10) adding the Anthropic-direct fallback to the frontier/standard classes in `rebar.toml` `[llm.model_classes]`. `_intersect_capabilities` in `src/rebar/llm/runner_support.py` intersects capabilities across the whole chain and collapses differing `prompt_cache_style` values to `\"none\"` — exactly the hazard the comment in `rebar.toml` around the caching keys warns about. So every call on a mixed chain runs uncached even though the primary Bedrock target supports caching.\n\n## Approach\n\nInvestigate before fixing (`/rebar-debug`): confirm with a unit reproduction that a chain `[bedrock:…opus, anthropic:…opus]` yields `prompt_cache_style=none` while the single-provider chain yields the Bedrock style; confirm from usage rows that the fallback almost never actually fires. Then pick one: (a) intersect capabilities only over providers that can actually serve the current call (primary first; fallback capabilities apply only after a fallback), or (b) make the chains homogeneous in `rebar.toml`. Default to (a) unless it destabilises the provider seam.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/runner_support.py`\n- `rebar.toml` (only if option b)\n- `tests/unit/test_runner_support.py`\n\n## Testing\n\nUnit: mixed chain keeps the primary provider's cache style until a fallback actually occurs. Live check: one `review-plan` after the fix shows `cache_read_tokens > 0` on second and later finder calls.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A regression test proves a mixed chain no longer collapses `prompt_cache_style` to none for the primary target; checked in `make test`.\n- [ ] After the fix, a production plan review logs non-zero `cache_read_tokens`; checked in `.rebar/usage.jsonl`.\n- [ ] The root cause and the chosen option are recorded on this ticket.","id":"96f3-af59-ba26-4159","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":["llm","cost","bedrock","prompt-caching"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Prompt caching silently disabled since 2026-08-12: mixed Bedrock+Anthropic class fallback collapses prompt_cache_style to none (~2x review cost)"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788029375846565150,"uuid":"40032e8a-3c4c-44ad-98e1-36e26bcbb5f5"}